  "recognized_text": "Small and medium businesses are told to digitalize before they have a clear next step. The hard part isn't finding another idea. It's deciding what happens first, what it depends on and what it may cost and which evidence supports the decision. A generic chat answer can sound confident and still leave those questions unresolved. So MagiPilot starts with 5 focused questions. Together, they create an editable business twin, a compact record of contracts, objectives, capabilities, process friction, constraints, readiness and evidence. Facts and unknowns remains visible. The objective is practical, which is to move from answers to an inspectable path, not just the paragraph of advice."
